Today's earlier merges all verify clean: 0610 (`tab_venues.md`,
`fig_traditions_pre2008_citers.png`), 0625 (`tab_network_limitations.csv`),
0640 (venue captions).

Findings that outlive this ticket, all reported rather than fixed here:

1. `fig_bars_v1.png` is not actually frozen. `manuscript.qmd` A.2 declares
   `@fig-bars` frozen on the first-submission corpus, but `plot_fig1_bars.py
   --v1-only` filters the live `in_v1` column of `refined_works.csv`, so the
   figure is recomputed from a mutable corpus; four year-bars moved. The
   committed PNG is the only record of the submitted figure.
2. `config/community_registry.yml` keys hand-curated community labels and
   colours on Louvain community *ids*. Its own comment warns they are stable
   only for a fixed seed; they are also only stable for a fixed corpus. On the
   pinned corpus 7 of 9 registered co-citation communities lose their name and
   colour, and `plot_fig_global_map.auto_label` renders three of them as the
   literal string `nan nan` (the ticket 0550 NaN-formatting class).
3. `tab_venues_fr.md` / `tab_venues_fr_caption.md` have no producer: they are
   hand-maintained French translations whose data body must be kept in sync
   with the generated `tab_venues.md` by hand. They match at HEAD; nothing
   would catch it if they stopped matching.
4. `tab_citation_verification.csv` is derived from a live-Crossref probe
   (`qa_citations.py`, 300 links) — the same class the author froze for
   `qa_cocitation_edges_report.json`. It reproduced byte-identically this time,
   so no action was needed, but whether it should also be frozen is an author
   call.

Prose that moves, for author arbitration (not edited by this branch):
`manuscript.qmd` A.5 quotes `84 nodes, 369 edges`, within-tradition share
`0.89`, null `0.37`, `z ≈ 25`, and "only about three co-citation-core nodes
match". The pinned corpus now gives 109 / 466, 0.878, 0.353, z ≈ 28.1, and
seven anchor nodes with eight edges.

`tab_null_separation_pre2007.csv` was regenerated, committed, and then put back
as committed. `tests/test_separation_provenance.py::test_a5_prose_matches_committed_csv`
reads those six figures out of the CSV and asserts each appears in the A.5
bullet, by design: the guard's docstring says a regeneration that updates the
CSV *and* the prose together stays green, and only a silent drift between them
turns red. Committing the CSV alone was that silent drift. So the artifact is
mechanically prose-coupled, the pair must land in one author-arbitrated PR
(0671), and until then the CSV stays as committed under the exit criteria's
"or carry an explicit author decision" clause. Worth recording as the general
shape: an artifact's *guards* say whether it is load-bearing for prose more
reliably than grepping the prose does.

Follow-ups filed: 0670 (community registry keyed on unstable Louvain ids, and
the `nan nan` label), 0671 (manuscript A.2 freeze claim and the A.5 numbers).
